<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lillie Langtry</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1853–1929</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Jersey Lily, Emilie Charlotte Le Breton</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lillie Langtry was a Jersey-born actress and society beauty, the daughter of the dean of Jersey, known as the Jersey Lily. She became famous in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> society in the late 1870s, was a mistress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a>, the future Edward VII, and from 1881 had a successful stage career in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. She was among the first celebrities to endorse commercial products.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lillie-langtry.jpg" alt="Lillie Langtry" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Napoleon Sarony · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lillie_Langtry_by_Sarony_cph.3b10327.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
